The outlier QC functions (`compute_row_outlier_scores`, `compute_subject_outlier_burden`, `drop_epoch_outliers`, `drop_subject_outliers`, `run_qc`) raise a `ValueError` when there are no features to score, for example `feature_cols=[]`. Without `group_by` every row scored 0 and QC passed with nothing checked; with `group_by` the call crashed with an unrelated `TypeError` or "No objects to concatenate".
